{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/120227-the-mummy-s-hand","id":120227,"title":"The Mummy's Hand","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-27T00:44:46-07:00","id":120227,"title":"The Mummy's Hand","content":"Hey all, I was looking over inspirational material for the M:tC and I happened onto <i>The Mummy's Hand</i> series of films by Universal studios. Stop me if this was already considered inspirational material somewhere else but...<br /> <br /> The movies follow Kharis, a man buried alive and cursed to forever hound and destroy those who would raid the tombs and treasures of Egypt. Kharis is kept alive by a race of priests (cult anyone?) that feed him a fluid brewed from tana leaves. A fluid of brewed from three leaves under the cycle of the moon keeps Kharis' immortality strong, while a fluid brewed from nine leaves will grant him movement and strength enough to destroy any who cross his path. <br /> <br /> Anyway, I was trying to think up something which could correlate to tana leaves in M:tC. I was thinking an ancient plant from the days of the Nameless Empire, or even a goblin fruit, which can be brewed into a soupy liquid by one's cult which could be fed to sleeping mummies and essentially help regenerate Sekhem at a faster rate\u2026<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T08:10:32-07:00","id":120343,"title":"","content":"The Mummy setting doesn't really have easy ways for mummies to regain S